    "blurb": "The set delivers strong performances of Casey Jones, Black Peter and Saint Stephen, with Bob Weir playing hotter than hell. Both soundboard sources are crystal‑clear, preserving the early‑70 energy and cowboy‑flavored vibe.",
    "review": "February 12, 1970 at Ungano's Night Club captures a snapshot of the Dead in their early‑70 stride – tight, energetic, and full of that raw New York club heat. Bob Weir is the standout, “hotter than hell” all night, driving the rhythm with gusto while the band rides through familiar covers like Casey Jones, Black Peter and Saint Stephen without missing a beat. The two soundboard recordings are both praised for their clarity – one described as a pleasant vault capture, the other crystal‑clear with an impressive crowd ambience on the finale of Casey Jones. Though no major musical missteps are noted, the show is best appreciated as a solid warm‑up that showcases the band’s developing chemistry before the epic runs later in the year.",
